WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:18.003
While the King was fetching the Executioner, Alice heard the Queen shouting.

2
00:00:18.023 --> 00:00:22.927
"It sounds like the Queen is upset," Alice said to the Cheshire Cat.

3
00:00:23.647 --> 00:00:25.429
"She's yelling about the croquet game."

4
00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:29.972
The Cheshire Cat's head floated above Alice, but he didn't reply.

5
00:00:30.916 --> 00:00:33.257
She decided to find out what was going on.

6
00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:37.980
The croquet game was as strange as ever.

7
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.161
"Off with his head!"

8
00:00:40.461 --> 00:00:42.803
the Queen shouted as Alice approached.

9
00:00:44.163 --> 00:00:45.904
The Queen pointed to another player.

10
00:00:45.924 --> 00:00:47.945
"Off with her head too!"

11
00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:51.567
"What did those players do?"

12
00:00:51.967 --> 00:00:53.308
Alice asked the White Rabbit.

13
00:00:53.328 --> 00:01:00.092
"They weren't paying attention, so they missed their turns," the White Rabbit replied.

14
00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:01.512
"Oh no!"

15
00:01:01.772 --> 00:01:02.333
Alice said.

16
00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:06.255
"I probably missed my turn when I was talking to the Cheshire Cat.

17
00:01:07.516 --> 00:01:08.717
I don't want to lose my head.

18
00:01:10.177 --> 00:01:11.318
I'd better hunt for my ball.

19
00:01:11.958 --> 00:01:13.539
I mean, my hedgehog."

20
00:01:16.321 --> 00:01:20.423
Alice quickly found her hedgehog, which was fighting with another hedgehog.

21
00:01:21.464 --> 00:01:23.125
She didn't try to separate them.

22
00:01:23.145 --> 00:01:25.486
"Where's my mallet?

23
00:01:26.187 --> 00:01:28.008
I mean, where's my flamingo?"

24
00:01:28.796 --> 00:01:31.959
She looked around and spotted her flamingo across the garden.

25
00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.423
By the time she grabbed it, the hedgehogs had stopped fighting.

26
00:01:38.845 --> 00:01:41.067
In fact, they were nowhere in sight.

27
00:01:41.087 --> 00:01:46.352
"It doesn't matter that they've disappeared," Alice said to herself.

28
00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.454
"There are no wickets anyway.

29
00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.776
All the soldiers have walked away."

30
00:01:51.617 --> 00:01:55.300
She tucked the flamingo under her arm and returned to the Cheshire Cat.

31
00:01:58.996 --> 00:02:02.218
She was surprised to find a crowd gathered below his head.

32
00:02:03.259 --> 00:02:05.140
There was a loud argument going on.

33
00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.922
The Executioner, the King, and the Queen were all talking at once.

34
00:02:10.843 --> 00:02:15.065
As soon as they spotted Alice, they turned to her and kept talking.

35
00:02:15.085 --> 00:02:18.867
"I can't understand you," Alice said.

36
00:02:18.887 --> 00:02:21.069
"Please take turns talking."

37
00:02:24.931 --> 00:02:26.552
The Executioner went first.

38
00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.102
"They want me to cut off this cat's head.

39
00:02:31.143 --> 00:02:33.805
But I can't cut off a head without a body.

40
00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:36.807
I've never done anything like that in my life."

41
00:02:39.628 --> 00:02:40.609
He crossed his arms.

42
00:02:40.629 --> 00:02:43.931
"And I'm not going to start now!"

43
00:02:43.951 --> 00:02:48.034
"Stop talking nonsense!"

44
00:02:48.655 --> 00:02:49.295
the King said.

45
00:02:49.315 --> 00:02:59.690
"All you need is the head, and you have a head here, which—" The Queen gave an impatient

46
00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:07.436
snort. "If somebody doesn't do something right now, I'll order everyone's head cut off!"

47
00:03:09.237 --> 00:03:12.880
After that threat everyone in the crowd looked frightened.

48
00:03:14.181 --> 00:03:16.983
Alice had a hard time thinking of anything to say.

49
00:03:17.903 --> 00:03:21.386
Finally she said, "The Cheshire Cat belongs to the Duchess.

50
00:03:22.187 --> 00:03:23.888
You'd better ask her what to do about it."

51
00:03:26.568 --> 00:03:30.832
"The Duchess is in prison," the Queen said to the Executioner.

52
00:03:30.852 --> 00:03:33.715
"Bring her here at once."

53
00:03:34.776 --> 00:03:37.518
The Executioner ran off to fetch the Duchess.

54
00:03:38.199 --> 00:03:42.203
The moment he was gone, the Cheshire Cat's head began to fade away.

55
00:03:43.284 --> 00:03:47.888
By the time the Executioner returned with the Duchess, the Cat had disappeared.

56
00:03:52.564 --> 00:03:57.767
While the King and the Executioner searched for the Cheshire Cat, everyone else played croquet.

57
00:04:03.531 --> 00:04:07.733
The Duchess tucked her arm into Alice's, and they walked away.

58
00:04:07.753 --> 00:04:12.596
"I'm so glad to see you again, my dear."

59
00:04:12.916 --> 00:04:14.898
The Duchess patted Alice's arm.

60
00:04:14.918 --> 00:04:18.280
"And I'm glad to see you," Alice replied.

61
00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.341
She was surprised that the Duchess was so friendly.

62
00:04:23.842 --> 00:04:25.683
Alice and the Duchess walked and talked.

63
00:04:27.023 --> 00:04:31.385
Alice wanted to ask about the Cheshire Cat, but the Duchess was busy talking.

64
00:04:32.325 --> 00:04:36.667
Suddenly the Duchess' voice died away, and her arm shook.

65
00:04:37.728 --> 00:04:41.289
Alice looked up and saw the Queen blocking their path.

66
00:04:41.309 --> 00:04:47.992
"A fine day, Your Majesty," the Duchess said in a weak voice.

67
00:04:49.248 --> 00:04:52.051
The Queen was not happy to see the Duchess.

68
00:04:52.071 --> 00:04:56.776
"Leave immediately or off with your head!"

69
00:04:57.437 --> 00:04:58.097
she shouted.

70
00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:04.684
The Duchess hurried away, and the Queen turned to Alice.

71
00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:07.367
"Let's join the game!"
